        <p class="profile-detail-region">Culture · Americas</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Caral–Supe civilisation</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Supe, Pativilca and Fortaleza valleys of north-central coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, 150–200 km north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a>, with sites in the Huaura valley; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caral">Caral</a>, Aspero, Bandurria, Huaricanga, Upaca, Vichama and Peñico.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">First city c. 3500 BCE at Huaricanga; large-scale building from c. 3100 BCE; greatest expansion 2500–2000 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caral">Caral</a> inhabited c. 2600–2000 BCE; decline from c. 1800 BCE.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the oldest known civilisation and city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>; earthwork platform mounds and sunken circular plazas; a society with no pottery and almost no visual art; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and fishing nets; bone flutes; a possible early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quipu">quipu</a>; no sign of warfare</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How we know them</span><span class="info-stat-val">Excavation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caral">Caral</a> and other sites by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruth-shady">Ruth Shady</a> from 1994 and by Jonathan Haas and Winifred Creamer; radiocarbon dates of shicra bags and other remains; plant remains, coprolites, pollen and bone chemistry; no writing that can be read.</span></div>
        </div>
